From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:01:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve an atomic inline's own intrinsic width keyword

taffy resolves min-content, max-content and stretch on a node's
children: block.rs and grid_item.rs do it for their items; and every
algorithm reading its own size style treats the keyword as auto. In an
inline formatting context blitz is that parent, so nothing resolved the
keyword at all: an inline-flex { width: min-content } shrink-to-fit the
line it sat on, 300px where Chrome and Firefox both say 140px.

Both measurements of an atomic inline have to agree, so they now share
one place that builds the inputs. The final stamping pass re-measures
the box to recover its border-box size, and measuring that one against
the line's space undid the keyword.

fit-content is deliberately left alone: an atomic inline is already
shrink-to-fit under auto. fit-content(<length>) stays unresolved too; no
browser sizes a box with it, and honouring it would have to answer for
box-sizing, which this path cannot see.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: upstream's inline_box_inputs already
resolves the width keywords (including fit-content) at both measurement
sites, after subtracting margins. Only the height half remains:
min-content, max-content and stretch heights resolve in
inline_box_inputs too.
---
 src/layout/inline.rs | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/layout/inline.rs b/src/layout/inline.rs
index 17bc625..75de5f8 100644
--- a/src/layout/inline.rs
+++ b/src/layout/inline.rs
@@ -38,8 +38,15 @@ fn subtract_margins(mut child_inputs: LayoutInput, margin: taffy::Rect<f32>) ->
 /// Layout inputs for an atomic inline box, with any sizing keyword on its `width` style
 /// (`min-content`, `max-content`, `fit-content`, `fit-content(...)`, `stretch`) resolved
 /// into the available space or known width the box is measured with.
+///
+/// `height` keywords resolve here too. taffy only resolves a sizing
+/// keyword on a node's children, and in an inline formatting context blitz is
+/// that parent: `min-content`/`max-content` measure the box against that space,
+/// and `stretch` fills the definite space left after the margins. Every
+/// measurement of the box goes through this, so both agree.
 fn inline_box_inputs(
     width_style: taffy::Dimension,
+    height_style: taffy::Dimension,
     margin: taffy::Rect<f32>,
     child_inputs: LayoutInput,
 ) -> LayoutInput {
@@ -78,6 +85,22 @@ fn inline_box_inputs(
         }
         _ => {}
     }
+
+    match height_style.tag() {
+        CompactLength::MIN_CONTENT_TAG => {
+            inputs.available_space.height = AvailableSpace::MinContent
+        }
+        CompactLength::MAX_CONTENT_TAG => {
+            inputs.available_space.height = AvailableSpace::MaxContent
+        }
+        CompactLength::STRETCH_TAG => {
+            if let Some(height) = inputs.available_space.height.into_option() {
+                inputs.known_dimensions.height = Some(height);
+                inputs.available_space.height = AvailableSpace::Definite(height);
+            }
+        }
+        _ => {}
+    }
     inputs
 }

@@ -430,7 +453,7 @@ impl LayoutPassState<'_> {
                     .intersects(StyleFlags::IS_BUTTON | StyleFlags::IS_BUTTON_INPUT);
             let contain_layout = box_style.clone_contain().contains(Contain::LAYOUT);
             let exports_baseline = !is_block_axis_scroll_container && !contain_layout;
-            let box_inputs = inline_box_inputs(style.size().width, margin, child_inputs);
+            let box_inputs = inline_box_inputs(style.size().width, style.size().height, margin, child_inputs);
             drop(style);

             if is_out_of_flow || is_floated {
@@ -987,7 +1010,7 @@ impl LayoutPassState<'_> {
                             .bottom
                             .maybe_resolve(container_content_size.height, resolve_calc_value),
                     };
-                    let box_inputs = inline_box_inputs(style.size().width, margin, child_inputs);
+                    let box_inputs = inline_box_inputs(style.size().width, style.size().height, margin, child_inputs);
                     drop(style);

                     if is_absolute {
